					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/yurmemir" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1607030); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1607030&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606661374" alt="Yurmemir" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1607030)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/yurmemir" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1607030); return false;" >Yurmemir</a></span> <span class="odate time_1386343700 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Dec 2013 15:28</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1909647">
									

<p>Not bad, but I just wasn't quite feeling it for a reason I can't quite put my finger on. Other than that, I do have a few nitpicks I'd like to point out:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">And&nbsp;nits&nbsp;shall&nbsp;be&nbsp;picked</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">And&nbsp;the&nbsp;picking&nbsp;shall&nbsp;thus&nbsp;be&nbsp;ended</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Face appears to have been removed,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The way this is worded, it makes it sound to me as though the subject's flesh composing his face was removed from his skull. I think something along the lines of &quot;Video of the subject has been altered to obscure the face, leaving a white silhouette blah blah blah&quot; would sound a bit better to me.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2000 is a set of 8 Cathode Ray Tube television sets,</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>All eight instances were deemed suitable for further study.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a bit contradictory. At the beginning you said that SCP-2000 was the designation for the eight units as a whole, while the second bit makes it sound as though each TV is an instance of SCP-2000. However you think best to fix that, it does mess with the article a bit as is.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Addendum 2000-C:</strong> [rest of log snipped for brevity]</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd just like to point out that while it is acceptable in articles to leave spaces between blackboxed words, when you have huge lines blacked out like in this log, it wouldn't make any sense for the person going through and blacking out all these words to meticulously go through and make sure he/she left every space between the words untouched. While it's fine to do it otherwise, it would make it more believable (at least to me) if the blackboxing in the log was continuous with no spacing.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I'm neutral voting for now. That might change as I mull it over.</p>

							</div>

								
					
