			<div class="content" id="post-content-1909975">
									

<p>I'm going to upvote assuming you'll take a look at my suggestions later.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>“Initially, while SCP-2000 was classified as Euclid, other, apparently failed, test materials were euthanized by the engineers of Mobile Task Force 43, ‘Quarter Junkies’.”</p>
</blockquote>
<p>-Your use of commas makes the entire sentence confusing. I’m having a hard time understanding what you are trying to say. Dragging it into Word and autocorrecting it comes up with this, “Initially, while SCP-2000 was classified as Euclid, the engineers of Mobile Task Force 43, ‘Quarter Junkies’, euthanized other, apparently failed test materials.”</p>
<blockquote>
<p>“The current status of SCP-2000 is unknown, as the anomaly it currently propagates makes future study difficult, to impossible.”</p>
</blockquote>
<p>-There is an overuse of the root word “current”. You are also relating the present with the future in a way that doesn’t really work.<br />
Rewording suggestion: “The status of SCP-2000 is currently unknown. The anomaly it propagates renders all methods of close examination with it to be non-viable.”</p>
<blockquote>
<p>“Personnel are advised not to listen to any possible attempts by former SCP-2000 researchers to contact them, and to immediately contact their immediate supervisor should such a situation occur.”</p>
</blockquote>
<p>-This is a bit of a run on sentence. Also you use the root word “immediate” twice in 4 words.<br />
Rewording suggestion: “Personnel are not to listen to any possible attempts by former SCP-2000 researchers to contact them. Personnel are advised to contact their immediate supervisor should such a situation occur.”</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;Research which led to the discovery of SCP-2000 was initially begun after an inquiry into the Unusual Incidents Unit&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>-Autocorrected in Word to: “Research, which led to the discovery of SCP-2000, was initially begun after an inquiry into the Unusual Incidents Unit”</p>
