			<div class="content" id="post-content-1910659">
									

<p>After re-reading, I am on the brink of an upvote. I just don't know what the hell is going on, and the article sure isn't telling me.</p>
<p>I don't know what the relevance of Site-92 is, I can only just barely discern what the CIA is doing, &quot;war simulation&quot; really intrigued me but is so obscured by the ending that it almost seems to be an afterthought&#8230;even though it's probably underlying the whole story! I just don't know what war simulation has to <em>do</em> with anything, and I can come up with two dozen wildly different answers on my own that are vaguely substantiated by the article. And I don't know, the vagueness just does not work out for me. The blackboxing frustrated me more than anything.</p>
<p>I really really like the CIA war simulation conspiracy with Atari angle, I just don't get enough of that angle for it to work for me. It's all hidden behind blackboxes and flat-out withholding of information, so I can't upvote. I don't have the information to tie everything together into one cohesive piece.</p>

